<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10497"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 2:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am posting this on behalf of another member who compiled all this info, I thought you would all find these predictions interesting. I did not compile this myself, just posting it for information and to answer a few questions that have been asked: <BR> <BR>listed below is some key points Dennis McKenzie told <BR>us about BTK on the chatsite catchbtk.com. <BR> <BR>White male, around 60 years of age, 5&#39;10&#34; to 6&#34;, <BR>stocky built. He was 59 years old, turning 60 in march <BR>shortly after his arrest. 5&#39;11&#34; and weighs 190 lbs. <BR> <BR>Dennis felt he used the number 3 intentionally. Turns <BR>out his birthdate is 3/9/45. Which are all multiples <BR>of 3. &#40;3X3=9 and 4&#43;5=9&#41; <BR> <BR>Den told us several times that BTK would be captured <BR>within the first part of the year of 2005. BTK was <BR>captured Febuary 26, 2005. <BR> <BR>He told us that his capture would be due to a slip up <BR>that would fall into the polices laps. And BTK sent in <BR>a floppy disc that he thought he erased info off of <BR>that traced back to him and his work for his church. <BR>Which led to the arrest of BTK. <BR> <BR>Dennis Mckenzie told us several times that he felt he <BR>did door to door labor at the times of the murders. <BR>Mentioned a van with a logo that looked like a sun. <BR>BTK <BR>worked for ADT Security systems at the times of the <BR>murders, and the logo from the company resembles a <BR>sun. <BR> <BR>Dennis said that BTK was a normal guy next door type, <BR>blended in with society, with moments of insanity. <BR>Also said he was a very neat person and liked <BR>everything in its place. BTK was definately a person <BR>that blended in, was even the president of his church. <BR>He was the compliance officer for Park City and took <BR>his job quite seriously, even measured grass length of <BR>people grass to make sure they were in compliance. <BR>Every one including family, friends and his pastor <BR>were totally shocked and had no idea Dennis Rader was <BR>BTK. <BR> <BR>Dennis said BTK didn&#39;t like dogs. Which i feel was a <BR>very key point since he also worked as a dog catcher. <BR>He had been known to let peoples dog out of their <BR>fence on purpose, killed peoples dogs, and reportedly <BR>had several dog collars and leashes at his home <BR>currently and sold some at his garage sales. <BR> <BR>Dennis said BTK was a wimp. BTK reportedly had a <BR>holier than tho attitude towards people he thought <BR>didn&#39;t live like they should. Harassed people that <BR>didn&#39;t comply with the laws of park city, was very <BR>strict in work, took his job very seriously. Like he <BR>needed to feel better than them and put them in their <BR>place. BTK is reportly singing like a bird since in <BR>custody.  <BR> <BR>Dennis Mckenzie told us of BTK home as being a white <BR>house, that sit back off the road. BTK&#39;s house was <BR>white and did sit back off the road. <BR> <BR>He also told us of his family, that he had a wife and <BR>2 children, 1 boy and 1 girl that were adults and <BR>lived out of state. <BR> <BR>Dennis said that Wichita Police Department new him in <BR>someway. With Dennis Rader being a compliance officer <BR>and a Sedgwick County dog catcher, i&#39;m sure he had <BR>contact with them in his job. Dennis Rader&#39;s name also <BR>appeared on some of the lists at the WPD they just <BR>hadn&#39;t gotten to his name to check it out. There are <BR>rumors that he&#39;d even been interviewed by them at some <BR>point...but i can not confirm this...it may only be a <BR>rumor. <BR> <BR>Dennis told of drops/communications from BTK before <BR>they happened. Even told us of a Doll that was in one <BR>of the packages left at Murdock Park.  <BR> <BR>Dennis told us at the end of 2004 that Marine Hedges <BR>and Delores Davis were Victims of BTK. Dennis Rader <BR>has been currently charged with their murders. <BR> <BR>Here are some other key points Dennis told us, that we <BR>really can&#39;t confirm as of yet, but may as information <BR>becomes available.  <BR> <BR>Dennis said he kept his treasures in a garage or shed. <BR>The police reportedly took several items from the <BR>house including from a rear shed attached to the back <BR>of the house and a detatched shed in the back yard. I <BR>am unsure if he had a garage at this point, but Dennis <BR>thought his garage was his darkroom. Dennis said his <BR>he had a brown leather type doctor bag with a brass <BR>latch, and a suitcase type bag with momentos. <BR> <BR>Dennis said he was frugel...very careful with money. <BR>We have no way of confirming this at this time. <BR> <BR>Dennis said BTK killed 13 people. He has been charged <BR>with 10 murders at this time. They are currently <BR>looking into other cold cases that could possibly be <BR>commited by him. Dennis said one was before the Oteros <BR>and with another MO, therefore that one may be harder <BR>to spot. There are 2 murders in close counties, Harvey <BR>and Reno, that the local sheriffs feel strongly that <BR>they may be BTK. <BR> <BR>Dennis feels BTK was mentally abused by his peers, and <BR>saw joy in the faces of the abusers. From what we have <BR>heard, he wasn&#39;t an easy person to work with in his <BR>jobs. Maybe it was due to his prior abuse by someone?? <BR>At ADT it was reported that none of his co-workers <BR>liked him due to his attitude. He didn&#39;t seem to like <BR>to be questioned on anything. Probably always thought <BR>he was right. He was the same with his job as a <BR>compliance officer. Anyone that got a citation from <BR>him said he even went to their house, even walked in <BR>their front door to remind them of court dates. <BR> <BR>Dennis McKenzies audios that are currently listed on <BR>catchbtk.com also have several points that the WPD <BR>have confirmed to him as being true.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
